# Line-ending policy for a cross-platform repo.
#
# Shell scripts MUST be LF: a CRLF shebang ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r") makes
# Linux fail with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory", and CRLF also
# breaks `tar`/`./install.sh` on some systems. Forcing LF here means a Windows
# checkout (core.autocrlf=true) can still be copied to a Linux box and run.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.desktop       text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf

# Everything else keeps git's normal text normalization (LF in the repository,
# platform line endings on checkout). Python is happy either way, and leaving
# it alone keeps the in-repo CRLF convention for syncplayer.py on Windows.

# Never touch binaries.
*.ico           binary
*.png           binary
*.mp4           binary
*.exe           binary
*.tar.gz        binary
